    "body": "## Motivation\n\nDeepSeek-V4's NPU RoPE cache retains contiguous FP32 real/imag copies after building the final interleaved cos/sin tables. These copies are only read when building a table; warmed forwards read the final caches.\n\nFor two frequency tables with 1,048,576 positions and rotary dimension 64, the unused copies occupy 512 MiB. This is a size calculation, not a whole-model measurement.\n\n## Changes\n\nKeep the real/imag copies local to `ensure_tables` so they can be released after construction. Final caches and the forward path are unchanged. Building another dtype regenerates the temporary copies at initialization.\n\n## Validation\n\n- CPU and Ascend NPU: 144 exact comparisons each, covering FP32/BF16/FP16, owner/no-owner, inverse, 4D, empty/repeated/changed positions.\n- Checked cold no-build rejection, warm cache pointer stability and nonpersistent buffers.\n- Two NPU graph replays with changed positions matched eager results.\n- Applicable formatting/lint checks passed. Two hooks could not launch `python3` on Windows; their scripts passed when run with the available Python interpreter.\n\nWith two 262,144-position tables, rotary dimension 64, and FP32/BF16 final caches:\n\n| Active allocated bytes above baseline | Before | After |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| NPU allocator | 671,095,808 | 536,876,032 |\n\nReduction: **128 MiB of tensor payload plus 2 KiB of allocator padding**. Measured with torch 2.10.0+cpu and torch_npu 2.10.0.post6. No full-model accuracy or throughput claim.\n\n[Reproducer, source snapshots and results](https://github.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/tree/9101e6fd8792ecffc4ad2a3a420176fdc46f6871) are on a separate evidence branch; this PR contains only the production change.\n\n![CPU and NPU validation results](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AkiYangDev/sglang/9101e6fd8792ecffc4ad2a3a420176fdc46f6871/validation.png)\n\nThe image is a report generated from the saved results, not a terminal screenshot.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->